Z||000000||FIEROCIOUS||06-02-2000||01:47 AM||||Does anyone know of any tricks or maintenance to make the Muncie 5spd shift smoother?<P>I purchased Rodney dickmans shift rebuild kit it was a quality product, however the new pin included in the kit is stainless steel and rodney made a coment on it wearing rapidly if in continous contact with steel? The original was hardened steel.<P>This concerns me but it was only 14.00 with shipping so I'll give it a try! Anyone had problems with this?<P>So is there anything else that can be done? <P>P.S. I use 5w30 sythetic mobil 1  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Will||06-02-2000||03:15 PM||||Have you tried using ATF?<BR>I use that and mine shifts beautifully (for a cable shifter).<P>If you want it to shift like a Ferrari you are probably out of luck.||||reg||1
